      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This Educational Bulletin discusses the effectiveness of hormone therapy (HT) for relieving vasomotor and urogenital symptoms and the side effects associated with such treatment; considers the evidence concerning the effects of HT on the risk of osteoporosis and related fractures and on the risks of coronary artery disease, dementia, and colorectal cancer; and considers the longer term effects of HT on the risks of stroke, venous thromboembolism, and cancer of the breast, endometrium, and ovary."},
